    "content": "I told our growth team they couldn\u2019t spend $100k on a Super Bowl commercial. Instead, they got Unify on ESPN's First Take with Stephen A Smith for $48.52.\n\nYesterday Ethan, Charlie and Madison came up to me in the office with a genius idea. With the Super Bowl being hosted in San Francisco on Sunday, ESPN was going to have multiple broadcasts recording live this morning.\n\nSo last night at 8pm, they ran out to multiple Walgreens to try to find one where they could get poster boards at. They were in the office till midnight making these signs.\n\nThis morning at 7am them (plus Neema and Owen) held up signs on ESPN like \u201cCold outbound sucks\u201d and \u201cOutbound needs a quarterback\u201d\n\nThis morning slot averages over 598k viewers, and people were coming up to them on the street immediately after the show saying, \u201chey I just saw you guys on TV!\u201d\n\nKiller work team, I\u2019m mind blown with this one \ud83d\ude2c",
